(Section 5: Paid Time Off \(PTO\) & Leave Coordination Rules) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
T*
T*
/F2 11 Tf
(5.1 Annual Accrual and Rollover Ceiling) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(Full-time employees accrue Paid Time Off \(PTO\) on a bi-weekly payroll cycle up to a) Tj
T*
(maximum standard allotment of twenty \(20\) days per calendar year.) Tj
T*
(\(a\) A maximum of five \(5\) accrued, unused PTO days may be carried over into the) Tj
T*
(following calendar year.) Tj
T*
(\(b\) Any carried-over PTO days must be scheduled and taken prior to March 31 of the) Tj
T*
(new calendar year, after which they expire without cash payout.) Tj
T*
T*
T*
/F2 11 Tf
(5.2 Non-Mandatory PTO Burn-Down Coordination) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(Employees taking parental leave, FMLA, or short-term medical disability are NOT) Tj
T*
(required to exhaust accrued PTO days prior to commencing statutory leave.) Tj
T*
(\(a\) Use of PTO during approved FMLA leave is strictly voluntary at the employee's) Tj
T*
(sole discretion.) Tj
T*
(\(b\) Front-line people managers may not mandate that employees burn down vacation or) Tj
T*
(sick banks before initiating FMLA.) Tj
T*
(\(c\) Unused PTO balances remain protected and intact during the full 12-week parental) Tj
T*
(leave period.) Tj
T*
T*
T*
/F2 11 Tf
(5.3 System of Record Filing via ADP Workforce Now) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(All life event leaves and PTO adjustments must be recorded through the ADP Workforce) Tj
T*
(Now API integration. Front-line managers must submit the approved leave schedule to) Tj
T*
(trigger appropriate payroll wage continuity.) Tj
T*
ET
